#todo("Problem Statement: What problem are you trying to solve?")
The main goal of this thesis is to expand the statechart feature/player experience module in pix:e to capture and analyze data that are helpful and interesting in the video game design process.

/ RQ1: Which data would be interesting?
/ RQ2: Which analysis of the data is interesting?

To this end, this thesis makes the following contributions:

- Path-based pacing diagrams in pix:e (@impl-diagrams)
- Modeling of lock-and-key puzzles and related solvability analysis (@impl-lk)
- User study to evaluate implemented features and identify gaps (@eval)

